    "long_instructions": "Welcome back! In the last levels, we learned that HTML is like a blueprint for building web pages and that the `<head>` section holds important information *about* the page.\r\n\r\nNow, let's give our web page a proper name! The `<title>` tag is used to define the title of the web page, which appears in the browser's tab or window title bar.\r\n\r\n1.  Open the `index.html` file.\r\n2.  Inside the `<head>` section, add a `<title>` tag. Make sure it's placed between the `<head>` and `</head>` tags.\r\n3.  Between the opening `<title>` and closing `</title>` tags, type an engaging title for your pet fish page. For example, you could use \"My Awesome Pet Fish Page\" or \"[Your Fish's Name]'s Home Page\".\r\n4.  After saving your changes, check your browser tab to see your new page title!",
    "generate_outline": "Students should add a <title> tag to their index.html file, placing it inside the <head> section. The title should be something engaging like 'My Awesome Pet Fish Page' or '[Fish Name]'s Home Page'."
